This is a utility to acquire information about recently approved applicants
who have passed the New Jersey's Department of Education's background check.

Really, this is just a proof of concept.  Eventually, the approval dates
will be added to existing information about applicants.  I'm not yet
sure where that information will be stored.  Perhaps a spreadsheet
in the short term but to evolve eventually into a database (if we
choose to create something fancy like an "applicant portal").

The container is started:

  docker compose --ansi never up --build

and then the utility is run:

  docker exec -it background-check-app bin/testGetForDate.0.py --days 10 --county cc --district dddd


to list approvals up to ten days ago where the list is in JSON.



To ease development, this does a little trickery in docker-compose.override.yml.
It mounts volumes containing the source code from the host.  This lets a developer
change and test code w/o rebuilding the container.
